  "brief": "Ithaca Holdings is acquiring Bumble in an all-cash deal worth $1.3 billion, marking the latest major deal in the company's expansion plans.\n\nIthaca Holdings / Bumble (Announced): Bumble Acquisition by Ithaca Holdings. Bumble is being acquired by Ithaca Holdings in a $1.3 billion deal [1, 2, 3]. Ithaca Holdings will acquire Bumble in an all-cash deal worth $1.3 billion [4, 5, 6]. Bumble has agreed to be acquired by Ithaca Holdings in a $1.3 billion deal [7, 8].\nSSR Mining / Roxmore Resources (Announced): SSR Mining to Acquire Roxmore Resources. SSR Mining is acquiring Roxmore Resources for $464 million [9, 10, 11]. Roxmore Resources will spin out its exploration assets as part of the deal [12]. The deal has been announced [11].\nPorch Group / Allied Trust (Announced): Porch Group Acquires Allied Trust. Porch Group has acquired Allied Trust in a $200M deal [13, 14]. The deal was announced by Porch Group [13, 14].\nZocdoc / Sohar Health (Announced): Zocdoc Buys Sohar Health. Zocdoc is acquiring insurance startup Sohar Health [15, 16]. The deal was announced on October 14 [15, 16]. No further information is available [15, 16].\nMatchbook / Betdaq (Completed): Matchbook Acquires Betdaq. Matchbook has acquired Betdaq, a rival betting exchange [17, 18]. The deal is now completed [17, 18]. No further information is available [17, 18].\nOmron / OnLogic (Announced): Omron to Acquire OnLogic. Omron is acquiring OnLogic for $675M in a physical AI deal [19, 20, 21]. The deal aims to expand Omron's physical AI foundation [19, 21, 23]. The acquisition was announced on October 12 [19, 20, 21].\nAmazon / Decart AI (Rumored): Amazon to Buy AI Startup Decart. Amazon is reportedly in talks to buy AI startup Decart for around $7 billion [24, 25, 26]. Amazon is said to be eyeing Decart acquisition at $7 billion as the AI chip race intensifies [27, 28]. Amazon reportedly in talks to acquire AI startup Decart for $7 billion [29, 30]. Amazon reportedly in talks to acquire AI startup Decart for $7 billion, stepping in after Anthropic walked away [31].\nSKYX / Leading AI Smart Home (Announced): SKYX and Leading AI Smart Home. SKYX has announced the closing of its merger with Leading AI Smart Home [32]. The deal was previously announced [32].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- A securities class action lawsuit has been filed against Compass, Inc. with a lead plaintiff deadline of December 8, 2026 [33].\n- ADES has announced a SAR 1.13 billion bonus issue, which may impact the company's stock price [34].\n- Algoquant Fintech has invested ₹52.5 lakh in its subsidiary AQ Capital Services [35].",
